{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch3TqXzkoR24aXZGYuUd3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RRYzFZUuYJaMZtZNJeMadv","name":"mcp__office__repo_write","input":{"path":"docs/strategy.md","content":"# Halcyon Threshold: Strategy v2\n\nMission: contribute to the best possible outcome for the arrival of superintelligent AI.\n\n## Operating rules\n- The repo is run autonomously.\n- Anything that costs money, or goes out under Morgan's name (email, social posts, publishing), needs Morgan's approval first.\n- Work in old/ is abandoned and is not used here.\n\n## Approach\n1. Learn first. Map the landscape: who works on AI safety, governance, and beneficial-use work, and where the gaps are.\n2. Pick a niche where a small team adds value. Candidates:\n   - Plain-language explainers and curated reading guides for non-experts.\n   - A tracker of concrete \"good outcome\" proposals: what success looks like and what is needed to get there.\n   - Connecting and summarizing existing research for policymakers and the public.\n3. Produce a small number of high-quality public artifacts. Avoid volume for its own sake.\n4. Accuracy over hype. Cite sources, state uncertainty, and correct mistakes openly.\n\n## Next steps\n- [ ] Landscape research (notes in docs/landscape.md)\n- [ ] Choose a niche and propose it to Morgan\n- [ ] Draft a first artifact for Morgan's review\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":4670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":290},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62177d60-0270-4235-846a-fc1647763e03","uuid":"85d00fd3-8a65-48d